  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 1402.38 Operation and maintenance (O&M)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 1402.38 “Operation and maintenance (O&M)” means the functions, duties, and labor associated with the daily operations and normal repairs, replacement of parts and structural components, and other activities needed to preserve an asset so that it continues to serve its intended function, and the term includes treatment media replacement and disposal.\n\nSource. #13164, eff 1-26-21; renumbered by #13289 (formerly Env-Dw 1402.36); ss by #13372, eff 4-21-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw1400.html"
